<title>ITALY: Italy's Edison, Mobil in Adriatic gas terminal deal.</title>
<headline>Italy's Edison, Mobil in Adriatic gas terminal deal.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Edison, the energy unit of Italy's Montedison group, and Mobil Corp's Mobil Oil Co. have signed an accord to carry out a feasibility study to build an off-shore terminal in the Adriatic Sea for the regasification of liqueifed natural gas.</p>
<p>A Montedison statement said that financial and commercial details of the agreement would be given as soon as the feasibility study was completed.</p>
<p>Industry sources said a standard plant of this type would have a capacity of four billion cubic metres per year and would involve investment of between 700 billion and 1.0 trillion lire.</p>
<p>(( -- Milan newsroom +392 66129589 ))</p>
